    "records": [
      {
        "id": "plan-reservation-lifecycle",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Reservation lifecycle",
        "text": "A reservation is **held** when checkout starts, then ends in exactly one of:\n- **committed**: payment authorised and the order saved;\n- **released**: payment declined or checkout failed;\n- **expired**: no outcome within 15 minutes, found by the sweeper.\nEnded reservations never change again. Fifteen minutes covers a 3-D Secure challenge (p99 four minutes) with margin.",
        "path": "plan.md",
        "section": "Reservation lifecycle"
      },
      {
        "id": "plan-data-model",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Data model",
        "text": "- A new `stock_reservation` row per order line per warehouse, referencing `stock_level (warehouse_id, sku)`.\n- `stock_level.reserved` holds the reserved quantity. Available stock is `on_hand - reserved`; checkout never writes `on_hand`.\n- Migration 002 only adds; old code keeps working against the new schema.",
        "path": "plan.md",
        "section": "Data model"
      },
      {
        "id": "plan-concurrency",
        "kind": "plan",
        "title": "Concurrency",
        "text": "All lines of an order are reserved in one transaction with a conditional update (`reserved = reserved + :qty WHERE on_hand - reserved >= :qty`). If any line updates zero rows, the whole order fails with insufficient stock and nothing is held.",
        "path": "plan.md",
        "section": "Concurrency"
      },
      {
        "id": "adr-reserve-at-checkout",
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Reserve stock at checkout, not when adding to cart",
        "text": "We reserve stock when the customer places the order, for at most 15 minutes, rather than when an item goes into the cart. Carts live for three days on average, so cart reservations would hold sellable stock for idle carts and need long expiries and their own abandonment handling. Reserving at checkout closes exactly the window in which the overselling happened. The accepted cost: a product page can show \"in stock\" and the customer can still lose the last unit at checkout. The low-stock badge on product pages softens this.",
        "path": "docs/adr/0001-reserve-at-checkout.md",
        "section": "Reserve stock at checkout, not when adding to cart"
      }
    ],
